A string begins with a __brivla__ if it does not begin with a ((Morphology: cmavo|cmavo)) and consists of any number of ((Morphology: rafsi|initial-rafsi)) (possibly none) followed by a __brivla-core__.

A __brivla-core__ is the part of a __brivla__ that carries the penultimate stress. It can be a ((Morphology: fu'ivla|fu'ivla)), a ((Morphology: gismu|gismu)), a ((Morphology: rafsi|CVV-final-rafsi)) or a __short-lujvo__.

A __short-lijvo__ consists of a ((Morphology: rafsi|stressed-initial-rafsi)) and a ((Morphology: rafsi|short-final-rafsi)).

''Note that a ''CVV-final-rafsi'' needs at least one ''initial-rafsi'' in front in order to constitute a ''brivla'', otherwise it will be taken as a ''cmavo''.''

-----------

A __lujvo__ is any __brivla__ that is not only a ((Morphology: gismu|gismu)) or only a ((Morphology: fu'ivla|fu'ivla)). 

